lding the bag when you think  about cash flow or income is that the  first thing like you need to have the  cash flow in order to be able to execute  any of these investing strategies  well you need  let's do it two ways one i don't like  deals where you don't get cash flow  right away that's why i'm not a big fan  of angel and investing we could talk  about that later but when it comes to um  investing today you i like to put money  down on the table and get money back day  one that's called cash flow investing  and we can talk about ways to do it it's  just that most people don't know how to  structure deals and i get it i only  learned this for being a private equity  but so so first thing is any deal you do  you should look for payment day one it  is not a good deal if you do not get  paid until 10 years because most angel  investments will go to zero not 100 x  and so you need to invest with that in  mind now you do have to have some money  to start investing typically or you can  use your sweat so it's either you have  equity or you have sweat equity and what  i talk to a lot of people about is even  if you're working with somebody even if  you have a job you like your job you  want to stay there you should be trying  to move towards ownership instead of  employment and you can do that as an  employee by asking for things like  revenue share where you take a  percentage of the revenue that you help  bring into the company or profit share  which is probably more likely  when you think about the first deal you  did walk us through how did you find the  deal  how did you negotiate it and then do you  still hold it did you think about  selling it at some point like how do you  think about like what the end of that uh  that investment looks like  yeah so the first deal that i did by  myself completely uh i still hold it was  a terrible deal i won't say the name of  the company because i don't want to hurt  the operator's feelings it was a  terrible terrible deal um